REV_S_GENERIC the problem is REV_TIMELY, and the introduction motivates it well.
REV_S_GENERIC the observation that PAPER_THING and SCI_THING are rarely studied together is a fair one, and the paper makes something of it.
REV_S_GENERIC the design of SYSNAME is simple and the paper explains it clearly in Section REV_SEC.
REV_S_GENERIC the implementation appears to be real, and the authors ran it at a non-trivial scale.
REV_S_GENERIC the evaluation covers EVAL_MEASUREMENT_UM as well as EVAL_MEASUREMENT_UM, which is more than most papers in this area do.
REV_S_GENERIC the paper is REV_WRITING and the figures are clear.
REV_S_GENERIC the idea of REV_KEY_IDEA_ING is, as far as I know, new.
REV_S_GENERIC the comparison against SCI_THING in Figure REV_FIG is convincing.
REV_S_GENERIC the authors are candid about the limitations of SYSNAME in Section REV_SEC.
REV_S_GENERIC the results in Figure REV_FIG are striking if they hold up.
REV_S_GENERIC the treatment of SCI_THING in Section REV_SEC is more careful than usual.
REV_S_GENERIC the paper takes a clear position and defends it.
REV_S_GENERIC the case study in Section REV_SEC is a nice touch.

